; pgBackRest runs as PostgreSQL's archive_command, in the domain postgresql_t,
; and pushes WAL to S3 over HTTPS (443) with credentials from the instance
; metadata service (80). Both ports are http_port_t. Measured on 16 November
; 2026: without this rule SELinux denies name_connect and archiving stops.
(allow postgresql_t http_port_t (tcp_socket (name_connect)))
